  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Hitsumabushi",
  "text": "Hitsumabushi\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n1 Unagi Kabayaki - Frozen Roasted Eel\n\nSake\n\nUnagi Sauce\n\n2 tbsp mirin,\n\n1 tbsp sake,\n\n2 tsp Usukuchi soy sauce,\n\n1 tbsp honey,\n\n1/3 tsp salt,\n\n400 ml dashi stock.\n\nSeasonings\n\nSansho Pepper Powder\n\nCrumbled Toasted Nori Seaweed\n\nSpring Onions\n\nWasabi Paste\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Pour 400 ml of dashi stock into the pan and add the 1 tbsp sake, 1/3 tsp salt, and a few drops of Usukuchi soy sauce.\n\n2. Stir, bring to the boil, then turn off the heat.\n\n3. In a second pan put 2 tbsp mirin, 1 tbsp sake, and heat. Lightly boil and let the alcohol evaporate.\n\n4. Add 2 tbsp regular soy sauce and honey. Stir, and bring the sauce to the boil. Remove from the heat and reserve.\n\n5. Coat the flesh side of the unagi with sake and grill with the skin side toward the heat until the skin becomes crisp and aromatic.\n\n6. Brush the skin side with sake and grill with the flesh side to the heat.\n\n7. When the flesh side becomes slightly brown flip it again for 30 seconds.\n\n8. Put the unagi on a chopping board and cut widthwise into 1/2 inch strips.\n\n9. Serve on rice dribbled with unagi sauce,\n\n10. Serve on rice with sansho pepper and toasted seaweed,\n\n11. Serve with rice, sansho pepper seaweed and dashi.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
